  "question": {
    "html": "<section class=\"context\"><p>A mass-spring system undergoes damped oscillations with a time period of 5.0 s. At t<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"=\"></span>0, the system is at maximum displacement. The graph shows the variation of the total energy of the system with time.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"a\"><p><strong>a</strong> Draw, on the axes, a graph to show how the potential energy of the system varies with time. [2]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"a.i\"><p><strong>a.i</strong> Calculate the Q factor for the system. [1]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"a.ii\"><p><strong>a.ii</strong> Draw, on the axes, a graph to show how the potential energy of the system varies with time. [2]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"b\"><p><strong>b</strong> Explain why engineers must consider resonance when designing structures. [2]</p></section>"
